WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:55.050
<b>Cutting Steel</b>

3
00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:55.830
No!

4
00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.800
Listen, Nami,
the Clima Takt is a weapon,

5
00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.000
but you have to rely on
a stronger one to use it:

6
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:00.870
Your brain!

7
00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.310
You gotta think to
survive a battle!

8
00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.510
Remember: Your mind
is the real weapon.

9
00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.580
Right! Think!

10
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.490
Let's see, I've got Heat
Balls and Cool Balls!

11
00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:11.660
All I need to do
is take advantage

12
00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.460
of their characteristics
and combine them!

13
00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:27.700
One last thing.

14
00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:29.140
Tornado Tempo!

15
00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.680
This is the centerpiece
of the whole weapon!

16
00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.810
Tornado Tempo?

17
00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.240
Okay, here's the deal:
As long as your enemy is human,

18
00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.190
they won't be able to stand
after being struck by it.

19
00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:42.250
But it's a last resort,
and you only get one shot.

20
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.250
If you miss, it's over.

21
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.190
If I miss, it's over.

22
00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.850
Pay attention.

23
00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.260
That little gadget
of yours is interesting,

24
00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.750
but it's not a weapon.

25
00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.000
Here's some advice, sweetie:

26
00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.340
If you can't use it to attack, it's nothing more than a toy.

27
00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.120
The day that thing can be called a weapon

28
00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.890
is the day you can finally hurt someone with it.

29
00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.200
Now...

30
00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.140
Stop running.

31
00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.810
If I don't do something quick, I'm gonna get skewered!

32
00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.210
The only chance I've got is that Tornado Tempo thing!

33
00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.000
If I can do it!

34
00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.350
Hey! Give that back!

35
00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.390
Did you seriously think you could kill me with this toy?

36
00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.020
Oh, please.

37
00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:33.740
A sweater can produce
more electricity

38
00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.880
than this little thing.

39
00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.950
Well, we won't know unless I try, so give it back to me!

40
00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.280
Come on, think!

41
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.850
I have to distract her somehow

42
00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.090
so she can't dodge
the Tornado Tempo!

43
00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.590
What do I have to work with?

44
00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.760
Uhh...

45
00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.960
There are the three different
types of air bubbles,

46
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.580
and the extremely dry weather of
this country, but that's all!

47
00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:00.950
If only there was just a little more moisture in the air.

48
00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.350
Wait! Moisture!

49
00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.120
That's it! This thing
has a rain technique!

50
00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.890
Rain Tempo!

51
00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.150
Water tricks?

52
00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:17.260
Rotating Sprinkler!

53
00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.290
Desperate.

54
00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.090
No, I'm not! I've got
a plan, you'll see!

55
00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:21.930
I don't think so.

56
00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.930
I've had enough of your party tricks.

57
00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.400
And speaking of parties, time to end this one.

58
00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.300
Uh-oh!

59
00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:35.320
Sea Urchin Stinger!

60
00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:42.390
Now why don't you be a good
little girl for me and die?

61
00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:54.740
If that'd been me instead
of the wall, oh, man!

62
00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.940
Since you showed me something interesting earlier,

63
00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:00.740
it's only fair that I return the favor.

64
00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.410
Now's my chance!

65
00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:15.270
Hot air rises while
absorbing moisture.

66
00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.370
When it collides with cold air that's descending,

67
00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:21.240
it rapidly cools, and the
moisture gets frozen.

68
00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.580
And then...

69
00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.520
Now Spike-Spike... Doping!

70
00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.420
I told you your life
was over, didn't I?

71
00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.260
Stinger Flail!

72
00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.020
At least you've proven that
you're a first-class expert

73
00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:57.590
at something, even if
it is running away.

74
00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.530
Oh, right! The air bubbles!

75
00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:09.900
A cloud!

76
00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:12.070
It's small, but it formed!

77
00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:13.910
Just what are you babbling about?

78
00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.480
It's still not large
enough, though!

79
00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.310
I've gotta make it bigger!

80
00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:20.420
Cool Ball!

81
00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:22.450
Heat Ball!

82
00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.760
I've had about enough of this!

83
00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.900
Time to die!

84
00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:35.470
Stinger Flail!

85
00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.480
Tell me. Are you
prepared to die?

86
00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:44.680
How 'bout you?

87
00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.880
You're just bluffing, girl.

88
00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:54.540
Am I?

89
00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.140
You're dead meat!

90
00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.250
What?

91
00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.320
Today's forecast
calls for pleasant weather

92
00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.420
with stable humidity and mild winds.

93
00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:34.460
However, a high-pressure
system will be moving in

94
00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.300
sometime during the afternoon.

95
00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.170
This could create
some strange weather

96
00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.840
in one particular area,

97
00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:43.700
so people in the vicinity need
to watch out for mirages.

98
00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:48.300
And more importantly,
for tornados.

99
00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.170
This is a centerpiece
of the whole weapon.

100
00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.210
But it's a last resort, and you only get one shot.

101
00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.740
If you miss, it's over.

102
00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:02.180
If I miss, it's over.

103
00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:05.850
A tornado watch has been issued!

104
00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.770
Something the matter?

105
00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:13.580
Oh, dear, it looks like

106
00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:16.510
that left leg of yours
is pretty injured.

107
00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:19.850
So much so, in fact, that I doubt you could run away.

108
00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:26.560
Sea Urchin Stinger!

109
00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:43.710
This is... It's nothing!

110
00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.610
It doesn't hurt at all!

111
00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.440
Do you have any idea
what kind of pain

112
00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:49.780
she's been going through?

113
00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.740
Compared to Vivi...

114
00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.740
Huh?

115
00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:57.780
It doesn't matter if I
lose a foot or a leg or two,

116
00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.750
or even an arm...

117
00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:01.820
I don't care!

118
00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.560
Now!

119
00:09:05.590 --> 00:09:09.900
Take this! Tornado...

120
00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.400
...Tempo!

121
00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:30.750
Huh?

122
00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:39.530
What? What? What? What? What?

123
00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:42.460
What have you done to me?

124
00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.710
It worked! I did it!

125
00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:58.750
Usopp! Vivi!

126
00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:10.530
<b>Battle Behind the Medi Assembly Hall</b>

127
00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:10.530
<b>Alubarna North Block</b>

128
00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.530
<b>Winner: Nami</b>

129
00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.790
What is he talking about?

130
00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:16.390
Pluton? What is that?
I don't have a clue.

131
00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:17.400
Pluton.

132
00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:18.630
According to legend,

133
00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:22.670
it can completely obliterate an island with just one shot.

134
00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:31.140
An ancient weapon
whose power rivals

135
00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.240
that of a god.

136
00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:33.810
It's somewhere in this country,

137
00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:37.150
but you already knew that,
didn't you, Your Highness?

138
00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:43.010
An ancient weapon?
Alabasta has such a thing?

139
00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:44.680
And father knew about it?

140
00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:47.720
Perhaps it is a secret passed down with the throne.

141
00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:50.990
Acquiring Pluton has always been my goal.

142
00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:52.190
With it, this peaceful country

143
00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:56.060
will become a military power to
be reckoned with under my rule.

144
00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.530
Your rule?

145
00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:00.560
You're not this
country's monarch!

146
00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:02.200
Oh, but I soon will be.

147
00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:03.270
And once I'm on the throne,

148
00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.940
it will be easy to bring all
the pirates in this area

149
00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:07.700
under my umbrella.

150
00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:10.600
With such influence,
eventually I'll gain more power

151
00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.790
than even the World
Government itself.

152
00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:15.060
No one will dare cross me.

153
00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:17.130
The World Government
would never allow you

154
00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.400
to wield that much power!

155
00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:21.310
You're right, they wouldn't.

156
00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.970
So where is the Pluton? Tell me.

157
00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.240
I don't know where you heard
that name, Crocodile,

158
00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:27.940
but I don't have
the slightest idea

159
00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.840
as to where it could be found.

160
00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:31.820
I'm not even certain it ever existed,

161
00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:33.970
let alone if it's hidden in this country.

162
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.000
It could be a myth for all I know.

163
00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:39.710
What you say probably isn't a complete lie.

164
00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:43.380
I have considered that possibility for a while now.

165
00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:45.310
That Pluton may have never existed.

166
00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:47.810
There are those who
believe it's just a fable,

167
00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:49.710
but I believe that it's real.

168
00:12:56.910 --> 00:13:00.220
What noisy insects.

169
00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.390
I heard that King Cobra's

170
00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:03.390
been crucified by
Crocodile up there!

171
00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:05.190
We've got to save His Majesty!

172
00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:06.780
If we can break
through those doors,

173
00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:08.450
we can save the king!

174
00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:09.980
How? We can't do anything

175
00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:12.470
because of those strange
hands coming out from them!

176
00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:14.810
It's impossible
unless we find a way

177
00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.960
to stop those things!

178
00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.190
If my timing's correct,

179
00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:20.290
the rebel army should break
through the defenses

180
00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.060
and reach that square in
approximately 20 minutes,

181
00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:26.120
where they'll clash with the royal forces.

182
00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:30.990
And then, in just half
an hour, at 4:30...

183
00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:34.990
...their battle will
be interrupted by a bomb

184
00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.010
I've ordered to be
fired into the square.

185
00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.210
Please don't! I'm begging you!

186
00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.090
Oh, and it's no ordinary bomb,

187
00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.260
but one so powerful it
will destroy everything

188
00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.460
within a five kilometer radius.

189
00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:54.400
If you do that, everyone...!

190
00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.430
That's right.

191
00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:57.140
No one from either the royal army

192
00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:59.270
or the rebel forces will survive.

193
00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:02.210
They'll be wiped out and the battle will be over.

194
00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.130
Aren't you happy? You should be.

195
00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:09.870
After all, you're the one who
wanted them to stop so badly.

196
00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:11.770
Since I'll be ruling from this palace,

197
00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:14.570
there's no need to blow it up just to end their fight.

198
00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:17.410
It's easier just blow
both armies up instead.

199
00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:19.440
This land's worth more than they are.

200
00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:22.340
How can you be so callous toward them?

201
00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:25.710
What did these people ever do
to you to deserve this, huh?

202
00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.980
They have lives and families!

203
00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:29.010
Princess!

204
00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.850
Who cares?

205
00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:33.120
You don't have to
kill them, Crocodile!

206
00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:34.720
Princess!

207
00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.360
Perhaps I'll change my mind

208
00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:39.210
if the king answers
another question.

209
00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:44.850
There's a Poneglyph in
this country, Your Majesty.

210
00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:46.150
Where is it?

211
00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:50.390
Poneglyph? What are
you talking about?

212
00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:53.990
If you promise to spare them, I'll tell you where it is.

213
00:14:55.780 --> 00:15:00.920
I'll... even show you.

214
00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.090
Father.

215
00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:09.100
Just what I'd expect from
a king. You're a wise man.

216
00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.940
Enough.

217
00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:15.470
I cannot take...
another second of this!

218
00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:35.040
<b>Medi Assembly Hall, Main Street
North Block</b>

219
00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:39.210
Shut up.

220
00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.880
Here, let me show you...

221
00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:44.590
...the difference
in pride between...

222
00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.560
...your swords and mine!

223
00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:51.430
Three-Swords Style...

224
00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:53.400
...Bull Needle!

225
00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.230
Spider...

226
00:15:58.230 --> 00:15:59.900
...Defense.

227
00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:18.220
Huh.

228
00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:21.590
So basically, your body is as hard as steel.

229
00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:24.860
Unless I can cut steel, I can't defeat you.

230
00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:26.980
That would be correct.

231
00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:30.920
Smashing and cutting attacks won't work on me.

232
00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.320
Well, that bites, doesn't it?

233
00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:36.290
I'm not capable of cutting steel yet,

234
00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:38.520
so I guess there's only one thing left to do.

235
00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:40.930
Hmph. And what's
that, swordsman?

236
00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:43.900
I'm gonna learn how
to cut it right here and now.

237
00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.660
Really?

238
00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.340
I've been waiting for a
challenge just like this one.

239
00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:50.970
I've been telling myself for a while now

240
00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:54.340
that it's time to take my skills to the next level.

241
00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:57.950
When I defeat you, Mr. 1,

242
00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:59.520
I'll be the swordsman
strong enough

243
00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:02.620
to cut through anything,
including steel.

244
00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.850
Huh. When you defeat me?

245
00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:21.180
That's rich. Ha.

246
00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.590
I hate to shatter your
delusions, pirate,

247
00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:25.420
but I feel it's only
fair to warn you

248
00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:27.860
that ever since I gained
Dice Dice Powers,

249
00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:29.290
I've never been scratched

250
00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:32.460
by those who call
themselves swordsmen.

251
00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:36.400
You'll soon see.
No enemy can defeat me.

252
00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:38.490
Ooh, I'm really scared.

253
00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:40.390
Save those stories
for your grandkids

254
00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:42.030
if you live that long, pal.

255
00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:44.500
Anyway, I don't know how many
swordsmen you've defeated,

256
00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:47.500
but you've never fought me before.

257
00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.330
So you better watch
what you say, big guy,

258
00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.740
'cause you're about
to eat those words.

259
00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:57.600
The only thing sharp about you is your tongue.

260
00:17:57.600 --> 00:18:00.330
All right, fine. I warned you.

261
00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:06.470
You won't last that long.

262
00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.510
Look who's talking!

263
00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:31.030
Huh?

264
00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.650
Oni...

265
00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:55.150
...giri!

266
00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:03.580
Tiger... Trap!

267
00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:36.710
I told you.

268
00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:41.150
Well,
I've gotta admit,

269
00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:44.480
I'm surprised you don't even have a single bruise.

270
00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:46.440
This is the first time this has ever happened.

271
00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:50.290
No opponent of mine is standing
after an attack like that.

272
00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:52.400
As true as that may be,

273
00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.360
you've never fought
against me before,

274
00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:57.270
so who's eating their words now?

275
00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:08.440
Oh, right!

276
00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:10.750
This guy's entire
body is a blade.

277
00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:13.980
So his blades don't have
a front or a back!

278
00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.990
Sparkling Daisy!

279
00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:29.600
This is crazy!

280
00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.040
Goodbye.

281
00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.840
When it comes to training...

282
00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:07.580
...I've done more
than anyone else.

283
00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:08.680
I've also been pushed
to the brink

284
00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:14.020
in plenty of bad situations,
but always succeeded.

285
00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:17.960
But what is it that
I lack to beat this guy?

286
00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:21.700
Sensei! Sensei!

287
00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:25.030
Hm?

288
00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:26.900
Is it true there are
swordsmen in this world

289
00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:28.870
who can cut anything,
even steel?

290
00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.640
Well, is it?

291
00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:36.500
Yes. It certainly is.

292
00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:37.600
Now pay attention.

293
00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:41.340
I want you to watch this paper very carefully, Zoro.

294
00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:46.550
Ha!

295
00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:48.950
Sensei, you didn't even cut it.

296
00:21:49.020 --> 00:21:49.920
Listen, Zoro.

297
00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:53.640
This is an important lesson for you to learn.

298
00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:54.860
There are swordsmen out there

299
00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:58.390
who are capable of
cutting nothing.

300
00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:01.700
However, these same swordsmen
can also cut anything,

301
00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:05.610
and that includes steel,
using the same sword.

302
00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:07.050
The strongest swordsmen
in the world

303
00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:09.650
are able to protect that
which they want to protect,

304
00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:12.420
but also cut that
which they want to cut.

305
00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.920
Swordplay that always harms
whatever it touches,

306
00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:19.900
well, Zoro, that's not
real swordsmanship.

307
00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:21.800
Do you understand?

308
00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:37.250
Sensei, I'm gonna be a
swordsman who can cut anything!

309
00:22:37.320 --> 00:22:39.020
Zoro, were you listening at all

310
00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:40.920
to what I was saying?

311
00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:45.210
Huh?

312
00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:55.120
Well, what are you waiting for?
Hurry up and attack me again.

313
00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:59.930
You'll never win if all you do is defend.

314
00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:01.130
Trust me, pal,

315
00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:03.900
there's nothing I'd rather do
more right now than that,

316
00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:06.900
but my hands are a little
full at the moment.

317
00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:13.240
And it wasn't a threat, it was a promise.

318
00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:17.110
I'm gonna cut steel
and you're gonna die.

319
00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:18.610
I highly doubt it.

320
00:23:18.640 --> 00:23:21.840
Shame you won't
be alive to see it.

321
00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:32.020
Large or small... I'll cut
everything into pieces!

322
00:23:33.320 --> 00:23:35.460
"Swordplay that cuts nothing."

323
00:23:35.490 --> 00:23:37.430
What the hell did that mean?

324
00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:40.360
Think!

325
00:23:40.740 --> 00:23:44.210
Cut nothing, but cut steel.

326
00:23:44.240 --> 00:23:48.010
It doesn't make any
sense at all!

327
00:23:48.050 --> 00:23:49.650
Thrust and thrust!

328
00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:52.320
That's the secret of
powerful swordplay!

329
00:23:52.350 --> 00:23:55.090
Atomic Spar!

330
00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:59.480
You're not the
only one who can cut!

331
00:24:27.340 --> 00:24:30.180
Crab... Grab!

332
00:24:51.400 --> 00:24:54.710
You're really starting to piss me off.

333
00:24:54.740 --> 00:24:57.080
The feeling's mutual.

334
00:24:57.090 --> 00:25:00.360
Perhaps we'd be evenly matched
if I were a pathetic swordsman,

335
00:25:00.400 --> 00:25:01.360
but I'm not.

336
00:25:01.380 --> 00:25:04.720
My weapons are far nastier than mere swords.

337
00:25:04.780 --> 00:25:07.280
Take this one, for example.

338
00:25:12.290 --> 00:25:14.430
Spiral Hollow!

339
00:25:18.460 --> 00:25:21.800
Jeez, what are you?
An excavator?

340
00:25:21.830 --> 00:25:24.270
An assassin, actually.

341
00:25:26.860 --> 00:25:31.200
Sparks? Just how fast
are those blades spinning?

342
00:25:33.200 --> 00:25:34.640
Oh, no!

343
00:25:36.310 --> 00:25:39.440
However, I don't mind being called an excavator.

344
00:25:39.480 --> 00:25:43.050
Because I'm going to be digging out your organs.

345
00:25:59.400 --> 00:26:03.730
There's only one thing
left for you after defeat.

346
00:26:03.770 --> 00:26:05.600
Death!

347
00:26:26.440 --> 00:26:29.040
I'm surprised you're still alive.

348
00:26:33.880 --> 00:26:37.120
I will not show my back to him.

349
00:26:38.620 --> 00:26:41.790
What are you going to
fight with? Your hands?

350
00:26:46.860 --> 00:26:49.130
Even if I tried to
explain it to you,

351
00:27:05.430 --> 00:27:07.530
Die in peace.

352
00:27:10.370 --> 00:27:15.670
I've had bad luck
with stones today.

353
00:27:26.400 --> 00:27:29.070
Go! Keep heading to Alubarna!

354
00:27:31.150 --> 00:27:35.790
I wonder... if the
rest of 'em... are okay.

355
00:27:44.620 --> 00:27:45.780
Hm?

356
00:27:51.890 --> 00:27:56.900
That's impossible. I cut
him so many times.

357
00:27:56.930 --> 00:27:59.830
Did he dodge all those falling stones?

358
00:28:05.670 --> 00:28:09.740
Is that what I did? Dodge them?

359
00:28:09.780 --> 00:28:11.140
No.

360
00:28:11.180 --> 00:28:13.980
I was just able to
sense the place

361
00:28:13.980 --> 00:28:16.580
where no stones would fall.

362
00:28:20.450 --> 00:28:22.520
My swords...

363
00:28:22.590 --> 00:28:27.600
One of 'em's underneath
that stone. I feel it.

364
00:28:29.960 --> 00:28:31.970
What is he doing?

365
00:28:40.470 --> 00:28:43.440
I've experienced
this feeling before.

366
00:28:47.200 --> 00:28:50.870
Everything goes
quiet around me.

367
00:28:50.870 --> 00:28:55.800
So quiet... I can hear my
heartbeat so clearly.

368
00:28:57.510 --> 00:28:58.840
Is this...?

369
00:28:58.840 --> 00:29:03.680
Is this what it feels like when
you're close to death?

370
00:29:03.780 --> 00:29:08.620
It was almost like... like those
falling stones gave me a hint.

371
00:29:08.630 --> 00:29:11.460
As if they were living things.

372
00:29:11.500 --> 00:29:16.200
No, it wasn't a hint. It was
much clearer than that.

373
00:29:16.200 --> 00:29:18.170
It was like...

374
00:29:18.260 --> 00:29:20.060
...rhythm.

375
00:29:20.120 --> 00:29:21.780
Could it be?

376
00:29:21.820 --> 00:29:24.990
Trees have their own rhythm.

377
00:29:25.070 --> 00:29:27.140
So does soil.

378
00:29:27.170 --> 00:29:30.240
Is that what it is?

379
00:29:30.270 --> 00:29:32.980
This is an important
lesson for you to learn.

380
00:29:33.010 --> 00:29:34.780
Zoro, there are swordsmen out there

381
00:29:34.810 --> 00:29:37.150
who are capable of cutting nothing.

382
00:29:39.250 --> 00:29:42.290
Does "cutting nothing"
mean hearing the rhythm

383
00:29:42.320 --> 00:29:44.820
of the things around you?

384
00:29:44.860 --> 00:29:49.160
If so, is that how
one can cut steel?

385
00:29:51.320 --> 00:29:53.690
What the hell did you do?

386
00:29:53.760 --> 00:29:56.830
After a vicious
attack like that,

387
00:29:56.830 --> 00:29:58.600
and all the blood you've lost,

388
00:29:58.630 --> 00:30:00.710
there's no way you
can still be alive!

389
00:30:00.710 --> 00:30:02.040
I hear it.

390
00:30:02.040 --> 00:30:06.550
His steel, it has a rhythm.

391
00:30:06.580 --> 00:30:09.650
Just like everything else around me.

392
00:30:25.570 --> 00:30:28.140
All right. Fine.

393
00:30:28.140 --> 00:30:31.310
When I'm done, you're gonna
wish you'd stayed down.

394
00:30:32.620 --> 00:30:35.590
Only one question remains.

395
00:30:35.590 --> 00:30:38.860
Do I really have the ability to cut steel?

396
00:30:38.890 --> 00:30:42.290
Well, there's only one way to find out.

397
00:30:42.360 --> 00:30:44.300
You failed with three swords.

398
00:30:44.360 --> 00:30:47.430
Can you defend yourself with only one?

399
00:30:47.630 --> 00:30:51.900
I won't... defend.

400
00:30:51.930 --> 00:30:55.600
So you're prepared... to die!

401
00:30:57.600 --> 00:31:02.610
One-Sword Style... Lion Strike!

402
00:31:02.640 --> 00:31:05.210
Atomic Spurt!

403
00:31:24.890 --> 00:31:27.990
Thanks to you...

404
00:31:28.020 --> 00:31:31.030
...I've finally reached
the next level.

405
00:31:35.560 --> 00:31:38.070
I don't know how,

406
00:31:38.070 --> 00:31:43.740
but he learned how to do it,
just like he said he would.

407
00:31:46.380 --> 00:31:51.450
Now that you've cut
steel, what's next for you?

408
00:31:51.510 --> 00:31:53.050
Diamonds?

409
00:31:54.860 --> 00:31:57.920
No, that'd be a waste.

410
00:31:59.920 --> 00:32:02.020
Good luck.

411
00:32:11.910 --> 00:32:22.750
<b>Battle in Front of the Medi Assembly Hall</b>

412
00:32:14.900 --> 00:32:22.750
<b>Alubarna North Block</b>

413
00:32:18.580 --> 00:32:22.750
<b>Winner: Zoro</b>
